ient\n4. \"又蹲下去\" - sufficient for the squatting\n5. \"用鞋尖把门口那滩雨水一点点刮进地漏\" - sufficient\n6. \"她伸手去按墙上的开关\" - sufficient\n7. \"灯没有亮\" - sufficient\n8. \"她没有再按第二次\" - sufficient\n9. \"而是走到走廊尽头\" - sufficient\n10. \"拧开应急手电\" - sufficient\n11. \"把光对准鞋架底下\" - sufficient\n12. \"左右扫了两遍\" - sufficient\n\nOK, these all look good.\n\nLet me also think about whether to combine \"顾晚晴走到走廊尽头\" and \"顾晚晴拧开应急手电\". The text says \"走到走廊尽头，拧开应急手电\" - these are two separate actions in sequence. They should be separate facts.\n\nAlso, \"把光对准鞋架底下，左右扫了两遍\" - \"对准\" is pointing/aiming, and \"扫了两遍\" is sweeping. Two separate actions.\n\nOK let me finalize. Actually, I want to reconsider whether the umbrella's dripping is \"正在发生\" or \"已发生\". \n\nThe text says \"还在滴水的折叠伞\" - the umbrella is \"still dripping\". The word \"还\" means \"still\" and \"在\" is the progressive aspect marker. So at the moment described, the umbrella was still dripping. This is an ongoing state at that moment.\n\nAfter she hung it upside down on the iron hook, the umbrella would presumably stop dripping (as the water drips off). But we don't know the timing precisely.\n\nI'll go with 正在发生 for the dripping.\n\nBut wait, the dripping might be relevant in the future. If the dripping continues even after hanging, that's a fact. But the text doesn't say that. So I'll just record the state as described.\n\nLet me also think about whether I should include the \"门廊铁钩\" as an environmental fact. It's where she hung the umbrella. This is a location detail. Worth including?\n\nI think the key environmental facts are:\n- The corridor light doesn't work (or specifically, the light controlled by the wall switch doesn't turn on)\n- The emergency flashlight exists and works\n\nThe wall switch not turning on the light suggests a power outage or burnt out bulb. The text doesn't specify the cause, so I'll just record that the light didn't turn on.\n\nOK, let me also think about \"她没有再按第二次\" - this is a clear negation. She did not press the switch a second time. The reason is implied: because the light didn't turn on, she decided not to try again. But the text doesn't explicitly state her reasoning.\n\nLet me finalize:\n\nActually, one more thing. The text says \"傍晚回楼\" - \"returned to the building in the evening\". This establishes a setting and time. Should I include the time as a separate fact? It's already in the action fact.\n\nAnd \"门口那滩雨水\" - there was a puddle of rainwater at the door. This implies it had rained. Worth including as environmental?\n\nLet me include it as a separate fact about the environment.\n\nHmm, but this is more of a description that sets the scene. The puddle is the reason she used her shoe to scrape it into the drain. The puddle itself is environmental.\n\nI think I have enough facts. Let me not over-include. Let me finalize the list.\n\nActually, let me reconsider one more time. The rules say:\n- 不要只抽主角 - don't only extract the protagonist\n- 也要抽配角行动、状态变化、认知变化、计划与承诺、关系与资源、规则与数值、条件与因果、否定、推测、误信、转述及来源\n\nIn this passage, only 顾晚晴 appears. There are no other characters. So all actions are hers.\n\nFor environmental facts, I think I should include:\n- 门廊有铁钩 (iron hook in porch) - she hung the umbrella there\n- 门口有地漏 (floor drain at the door) - she scraped water into it\n- 走廊尽头有应急手电 (emergency flashlight at corridor end) - she turned it on\n- 墙上有开关 (wall switch) - she pressed it\n- 鞋架 (shoe rack) - she checked under it\n\nThese are environmental features that might be referenced in future chapters. Let me include them as separate facts.\n\nActually, hmm. The text doesn't say these features are \"in the building\" or are \"permanent\". They are just mentioned in passing. I think I can include them as environmental facts.\n\nLet me add a few:\n\n- 门廊有一个铁钩，用于挂伞\n- 门口有一个地漏\n- 楼道有一个墙上的开关\n- 走廊有一个尽头\n- 走廊尽头有一支应急手电\n- 楼里有一个鞋架\n\nThese are environmental. But are they really worth extracting? The rule says to extract things that \"以后可能被检索或续写使用\".\n\nI think the most useful ones are