\"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"拧开应急手电\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"顾晚晴把应急手电的光对准鞋架底下\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"把光对准鞋架底下\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"顾晚晴在鞋架底下左右扫了两遍\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"左右扫了两遍\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nWait, I should also think about: the protagonist is implied to be checking under the shoe rack with a flashlight. Why? We don't know - she might be looking for something. But the text doesn't say. So I shouldn't speculate.\n\nLet me also think about whether \"她伸手去按墙上的开关\" is exactly \"她去按\" or \"她按\". The text says \"她伸手去按\" - she reached out to press. The \"去\" suggests intent, but the action of pressing seems to have happened (the next clause is \"灯没有亮\", implying the press did occur). So 已发生.\n\nActually, \"伸手去按\" could be interpreted as \"reached out to press\" - the reaching happened, and the pressing happened. Both are 已发生.\n\nOK, I think my list is good. Let me also think about whether to add:\n\n- \"门口有一滩雨水\" - there was a puddle of rainwater at the door\n  Status: 已发生 (this is describing a past state)\n  Evidence: \"门口那滩雨水\"\n\n- \"楼里停电了\" or \"墙上开关失灵\" - inferred from \"灯没有亮\"\n  But the text doesn't say this, so I shouldn't include it.\n\nLet me think about whether \"门口有一滩雨水\" is worth including. The puddle is part of the context. The act of scraping it is the action. The puddle itself is environmental.\n\nI'll skip it as it's not directly relevant for future reference.\n\nLet me also think: \"门廊铁钩\" - the iron hook. Is it specifically for umbrellas? The text doesn't say, just that the umbrella was hung on it. So \"门廊有一个铁钩\" is the fact, not \"for umbrellas\".\n\nOK, I think I'll include some environmental facts as well. Let me add a few:\n\n- \"门廊有一个铁钩\" - already happened (it exists)\n- \"门口有一个地漏\" - already happened\n- \"楼道墙上有开关\" - already happened\n- \"走廊尽头有应急手电\" - already happened (implied by her turning it on there)\n- \"楼里有一个鞋架\" - already happened